Axn standalone message resolution
  an unconditional dynamic message is a headline by default (handler kind is irrelevant)
    is expected to eq "raw boom"
  custom join on the base
    is expected to eq "Couldn't sync user — is invalid"
  no reason matches → base shown alone
    is expected to eq "Couldn't sync user"
  prebuilt conditional descriptor is attached to the base (like the DSL)
    is expected to eq "Base: invalid"
  a headline block that RAISES falls back to an earlier headline (and that headline's join)
    is expected to eq "Earlier base: detail"
  no base declared (gate closed)
    is expected to eq "is invalid"
  reason opted out with standalone: true
    is expected to eq "Vendor not found"
  join comes from the headline that actually resolved, not a blank newer one
    is expected to eq "Base: detail"
  explicit empty join (no separator)
    is expected to eq "Failedreason"
  when multiple conditional reasons match, the most-recently-declared wins
    is expected to eq "Base: specific"
  unconditional dynamic detail with a base (promoted via standalone: false)
    is expected to eq "Couldn't sync user: boom"
  a declared-but-blank base still gates reasons as attached, then drops the empty base
    is expected to eq "lonely reason"
  declared reason with a base (attached by default)
    is expected to eq "Couldn't sync user: is invalid"
  an unconditional dynamic message is attached only when promoted with standalone: false
    is expected to eq "Import failed: raw boom"

